---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const sample = `In today's rapidly evolving digital landscape, it is important to note that effective communication is more crucial than ever. This revolutionary approach seamlessly empowers teams to unlock their full potential.

It's not merely a writing tool, it's a paradigm shift. Ultimately, the future of clear communication is here.`;
---

<SiteLayout>
  <header class="site-header">
    <a class="wordmark" href="#top" aria-label="SlopSift home">
      <span>slop</span><span>sift</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </a>
    <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
      <a href="#demo">Try it</a>
      <a href="#surfaces">Tools</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/NikhilVerma/writinglint">GitHub</a>
      <a class="nav-install" href="#install">Install</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <p class="kicker">The AI slop linter</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Your AI<br />has a tell.</h1>
        <p class="hero__summary">SlopSift catches the canned structure, borrowed certainty, and suspiciously polished filler that spellcheck misses.</p>
        <div class="hero__actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="#demo">Lint some text</a>
          <button class="install-command" type="button" data-copy="bunx slopsift ." aria-label="Copy install command">
            <code>bunx slopsift .</code><span>copy</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="proof-sheet" aria-label="An example paragraph marked up by SlopSift">
        <div class="proof-sheet__top">
          <span>draft_07.md</span><span>6 problems</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          <span class="proof proof--error">In today’s rapidly evolving landscape,<b>delete the canned opening</b></span>
          clear writing is
          <span class="proof proof--warning">more important than ever.<b>compared with what?</b></span>
        </p>
        <p>
          This <span class="proof proof--note">revolutionary approach<b>promotional vocabulary</b></span>
          <span class="proof proof--error">seamlessly empowers teams<b>say what it does</b></span>
          to unlock their full potential.
        </p>
        <div class="proof-sheet__score"><strong>38</strong><span>Reads like a press release written by a toaster.</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="rule-ticker" aria-label="Examples of SlopSift rules">
      <span>corrective-antithesis</span><span>unsupported-certainty</span><span>mechanical-outline</span><span>vague-attribution</span><span>ai-vocabulary</span>
    </div>

    <section class="demo-section" id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="kicker">No account. No upload.</p>
        <h2 id="demo-title">Paste the evidence.</h2>
        <p>The same compact parser used by the CLI runs in your browser. Your draft stays on your device.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lint-demo" data-slop-demo>
        <div class="lint-demo__editor">
          <div class="panel-bar"><span>INPUT</span><span>plain text</span></div>
          <textarea aria-label="Text to lint" spellcheck="true">{sample}</textarea>
          <div class="demo-controls">
            <p data-status>Ready when you are.</p>
            <button class="button button--primary" type="button" data-run>Run SlopSift</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lint-demo__results">
          <div class="panel-bar"><span>PROBLEMS</span><span data-totals>not linted yet</span></div>
          <div class="results-list" data-results aria-live="polite">
            <p class="results-empty">Run the sample to load the local parser.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div class="method__intro">
        <h2 id="method-title">It reads structure,<br />not vibes.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="method__steps">
        <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Parse the sentence</h3><p>A small owned model maps words, parts of speech, and grammatical relationships.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Run explainable rules</h3><p>Each finding names the construction it matched. No mystery score. No remote judge.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Grade the suspicion</h3><p>Errors are strong tells. Warnings need attention. Notes are candidates, not convictions.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="severity" aria-labelledby="severity-title">
      <div class="severity__title">
        <h2 id="severity-title">Not every dash is a crime.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="severity__examples">
        <article class="severity-row severity-row--error"><span>error</span><p>“As an AI language model...”</p><strong>caught red-handed</strong></article>
        <article class="severity-row severity-row--warning"><span>warning</span><p>Three paragraphs use the same canned outline.</p><strong>probably slop</strong></article>
        <article class="severity-row severity-row--note"><span>note</span><p>An actorless passive may be hiding responsibility.</p><strong>worth a look</strong></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="surfaces" id="surfaces" aria-labelledby="surfaces-title">
      <div class="section-heading section-heading--compact">
        <h2 id="surfaces-title">Meet writers where they write.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="surface-list">
        <article><div class="surface-mark">$</div><div><h3>CLI</h3><p>Glob files, lint Markdown, inspect code comments, and emit ESLint-shaped JSON in CI.</p></div><code>bunx slopsift .</code></article>
        <article><div class="surface-mark">VS</div><div><h3>VS Code</h3><p>Diagnostics appear beside the sentence, with the same severity and rule name as the terminal.</p></div><span>local</span></article>
        <article><div class="surface-mark">CR</div><div><h3>Chrome</h3><p>Review text boxes and editable pages before the draft escapes into the internet.</p></div><span>private</span></article>
        <article><div class="surface-mark">AI</div><div><h3>Agent skill</h3><p>Let coding agents lint their own prose before they hand it back to a human.</p></div><span>coming next</span></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="manifesto">
      <p class="manifesto__aside">Yes, AI helped build this.</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Built by AI.<br /><span>Edited on purpose.</span></h2>
        <p>That is the point. SlopSift is not an AI detector and it does not pretend to know who typed a sentence. It catches habits that make writing vague, inflated, repetitive, or weirdly certain. Human beings do those things too.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="install-title">One command.<br />Several opinions.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal" role="group" aria-label="Install SlopSift">
        <div class="terminal__bar"><span>terminal</span><span>~/your-writing</span></div>
        <button type="button" data-copy="bunx slopsift ."><span>$</span><code>bunx slopsift .</code><b>copy</b></button>
        <p>Use <code>--format json</code> for machines, <code>--level info</code> for the full suspicious pile.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <a class="wordmark" href="#top"><span>slop</span><span>sift</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
    <p>Open source. Local first. Opinionated by design.</p>
    <div><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a><a href="https://github.com/NikhilVerma/writinglint">GitHub</a><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/slopsift">npm</a></div>
  </footer>

  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-copy]').forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copy);
        } catch {
          return;
        }
        const label = button.querySelector('span:last-child, b');
        if (!label) return;
        const before = label.textContent;
        label.textContent = 'copied';
        window.setTimeout(() => { label.textContent = before; }, 1200);
      });
    });
  </script>
  <script type="module" src="/demo.js"></script>
</SiteLayout>
